{
  "title": "Sync cursors silently stop syncing after a database dump/restore",
  "description": "Recipe and shopping-list sync cursors are raw Postgres transaction ids (pg_current_xact_id(), migrations 2026-07-12 sync_change_xid and 2026-10-11 shopping_list_change_xid; server/src/api/shopping_list/sync.rs, server/src/api/recipes/sync.rs). \
A logical dump/restore or a move to a new cluster restarts the xid counter low, so clients keep cursors above every new change_xid and never receive new changes, with no error. \
Fix: in both sync handlers, treat a cursor above pg_snapshot_xmax(pg_current_snapshot()) as invalid and do a full resync, with an e2e test that sends an impossibly high cursor. \
This may be subsumed by blocked-one-sync-mechanism; fix it there if that lands first.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 3,
  "type": "bug",
  "labels": [
    "api",
    "sync",
  ],
  "created_at": "2026-10-11T08:00:00-07:00",
